# Horizon — Focus Resilience Meter

A dashboard prototype for the "Attention Span & Focus Resilience Meter" concept: a horizon-line dial where the sun's position stands in for current focus quality, plus a session mode, weekly trends, and a calibration probe.

## Run it

No build step — plain HTML/CSS/JS.

1. Open this folder in VS Code.
2. Install the **Live Server** extension (if you don't have it).
3. Right-click `index.html` → **Open with Live Server**.

Or just double-click `index.html` to open it directly in a browser.

## Files

- `index.html` — structure for all four screens (Home, Session, Trends, Settings)
- `style.css` — design tokens (colors, type, spacing) and layout
- `app.js` — dial rendering, simulated live data, session timer, trends chart, attention probe

## Where the real data would plug in

Everything is currently simulated with `Math.random()` so the UI has believable numbers to show. To wire it to real signals, replace:

- `currentScore` random walk → your actual focus-quality model output
- `dayScores` in the Trends tab → aggregated daily scores from stored sessions
- the attention probe's reaction-time capture → feed its output into your calibration model instead of just displaying the average

The layout assumes on-device processing (see the sources panel in Settings) — nothing here calls an external API.
